-- On Linux with kernel.perf_event_paranoid set to 4, at which an Ubuntu
-- kernel refuses the events to every process without privileges, as CI
-- sets it on its Ubuntu runners: the error, the error of the system,
-- and the hint.
EXPLAIN (ANALYZE, PMU) SELECT 1;
ERROR:  the system does not allow this process to count instructions
DETAIL:  The system said: Permission denied.
HINT:  On Linux, set kernel.perf_event_paranoid to 2 or less, or give the server's processes CAP_PERFMON; in a container, its filter of system calls may refuse perf_event_open too.
